          <span class="ed-method">Based on published exercise guidance. General information, not medical advice.</span>
        </div>
        <a href="#short-answer" class="btn-ghost">The Short Answer</a>
      </div>
      <p class="ed-disclosure">
        Nothing on this page is a paid placement, and it carries no affiliate links. <a href="/editorial-standards/">How we review.</a>
      </p>

      <div class="ed-body prose prose-lg">
        <p class="ed-lead">
          Running plans, race goals and running apps all talk in minutes per mile. The treadmill
          console talks in miles per hour. Translating one into the other is simple arithmetic, but
          it is the kind of arithmetic nobody wants to do while the belt is already moving. Here are
          the answers worked out, plus what to set when your target pace does not land on a round
          number.
        </p>

